\section*{Question 5}

A coffeepot has the shape of a cylinder with radius 5 inches, as shown in the figure above. Let \(h\) be the depth of the coffee in the pot, measured in inches, where \(h\) is a function of time \(t\), measured in seconds. The volume \(V\) of coffee in the pot is changing at the rate of \(-5 \pi \sqrt{h}\) cubic inches per second. (The volume \(V\) of a cylinder with radius \(r\) and height \(h\) is \(V=\pi r^{2} h\).)
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Show that \(\frac{d h}{d t}=-\frac{\sqrt{h}}{5}\).
\item[(b)] Given that \(h=17\) at time \(t=0\), solve the differential equation \(\frac{d h}{d t}=-\frac{\sqrt{h}}{5}\) for \(h\) as a function of \(t\).
\item[(c)] At what time \(t\) is the coffeepot empty?
\item[(a)] \(V=25 \pi h\)
\[
\begin{aligned}
& \frac{d V}{d t}=25 \pi \frac{d h}{d t}=-5 \pi \sqrt{h} \\
& \frac{d h}{d t}=\frac{-5 \pi \sqrt{h}}{25 \pi}=-\frac{\sqrt{h}}{5}
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(b)] \(\frac{d h}{d t}=-\frac{\sqrt{h}}{5}\)
\[
\begin{aligned}
& \frac{1}{\sqrt{h}} d h=-\frac{1}{5} d t \\
& 2 \sqrt{h}=-\frac{1}{5} t+C \\
& 2 \sqrt{17}=0+C
\end{aligned}
\]
\[
h=\left(-\frac{1}{10} t+\sqrt{17}\right)^{2}
\]
\end{itemize}
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/5f2d7e45-ff03-41a1-99fa-a997d2871d77-1.jpg?height=589&width=357&top_left_y=385&top_left_x=1616)
\begin{itemize}
\item[] \(3:\left\{\begin{array}{l}1: \frac{d V}{d t}=-5 \pi \sqrt{h} \\ 1: \text { computes } \frac{d V}{d t} \\ 1: \text { shows result }\end{array}\right.\)
\item[] \(5:\left\{\begin{array}{l}1: \text { separates variables } \\ 1: \text { antiderivatives } \\ 1: \text { constant of integration } \\ 1: \text { uses initial condition } h=17 \\ \quad \text { when } t=0 \\ 1: \text { solves for } h\end{array}\right.\)
\end{itemize}

Note: \(\max 2 / 5[1-1-0-0-0]\) if no constant of integration

Note: 0/5 if no separation of variables

1 : answer
\begin{itemize}
\item[(c)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
& \left(-\frac{1}{10} t+\sqrt{17}\right)^{2}=0 \\
& t=10 \sqrt{17}
\end{aligned}
\]
\end{itemize}
